<title>UK: Chrysler eyes $200 mln three-yr Eurobond - UBS.</title>
<headline>Chrysler eyes $200 mln three-yr Eurobond - UBS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler Corp is expected to launch a $200 million retail-targeted three-year Eurobond, a syndicate manager at UBS said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are talking with them about doing a deal,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The amount is expected to be for around $200 million at a three-year maturity, he said.</p>
<p>Chrysler is a rare issuer in the Eurobond market and will be priced in comparison with other car companies such as Ford and GMAC, the syndicate manager said.</p>
<p>Traders said a launch spread in the mid- to low 20's basis points over U.S. Treasuries was likely.</p>
<p>-- Hayley Pienaar, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
